DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     Function ddwwaarrff__llnnee__eenndd__sseeqquueennccee() sets the address that indicates the end
     of a sequence of target machine instructions.

     Argument _d_b_g should reference a DWARF producer instance allocated using
     dwarf_producer_init(3) or dwarf_producer_init_b(3).

     Argument _a_d_d_r specifies an address value which is the first byte after
     the end of a instruction sequence.

     If argument _e_r_r is not NULL, it will be used to store error information
     in case of an error.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     On success, function ddwwaarrff__llnnee__eenndd__sseeqquueennccee() returns DW_DLV_OK.  In case
     of an error, function ddwwaarrff__llnnee__eenndd__sseeqquueennccee() returns DW_DLV_NOCOUNT and
     sets the argument _e_r_r.

EERRRROORRSS
     Function ddwwaarrff__llnnee__eenndd__sseeqquueennccee() can fail with:

     [DW_DLE_ARGUMENT]  Argument _d_b_g was NULL.

     [DW_DLE_ARGUMENT]  The value in argument _a_d_d_r overlapped an existing line
                        information entry.

     [DW_DLE_MEMORY]    An out of memory condition was encountered during the
                        execution of the function.

